  "facts": [
    "Opened on February 1, 1991, the Meghna Bridge was Japan's largest aid project worldwide, funded by the Japanese government and engineered by Nippon Koei Co. Ltd.",
    "Spanning 930 metres with thirteen cantilever spans, the Meghna Bridge features 11‑metre‑long hexagonal piers and 9.2‑metre‑wide dual carriageways, each side flanked by 0.8‑metre sidewalks.",
    "After 2005 and again in 2012‑13, extensive repairs replaced damaged expansion joints and protected piers from scour, ensuring the bridge’s continued resilience over the Meghna River."
